      "message": "Drive by: I think we should use the virtual method `PreferNotUsingMappableOrUniformBufferAsStorage` for this purpose, instead of adding another condition check here.\nIf a backend doesn\u0027t support mappable storable buffers, its `PreferNotUsingMappableOrUniformBufferAsStorage` implementation should return true.\n\nThe virtual method was originally created for this, but it\u0027s only implemented in D3D11 backend atm.\n\nIMO it also doesn\u0027t make sense to check whether the `BufferMapExtendedUsages` feature is enabled here. A backend might support it natively but the user just doesn\u0027t enable it. In that case, it\u0027s still ok to create a mappable buffer with the internal storage usage.",
